  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "enterprise_brief_chunk_0",
      "text": "Nexus-GraphRAG is an open-source Python framework developed by Nitesh Beniwal in Jaipur, Rajasthan. It bridges the gap between unstructured document collections and structured graph reasoning. The architecture combines NetworkX, NumPy, and Scikit-learn algorithms with modern Generative AI pipelines. Traditional vector databases struggle with holistic questions and multi-hop relationships.",
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "metadata": {
        "doc_id": "enterprise_brief"
      },
      "token_count": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "enterprise_brief_chunk_1",
      "text": "Nexus-GraphRAG solves this by implementing dual-mode extraction: a 100% offline deterministic extractor\nand an optional Google Gemini 2.0 Flash LLM extractor. The engine segments documents into overlapping chunks, discovers entities, and builds typed relational edges. Once the knowledge graph is constructed, Louvain modularity partitions interconnected nodes into semantic communities.",
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "doc_id": "enterprise_brief"
      },
      "token_count": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "enterprise_brief_chunk_2",
      "text": "Nexus-GraphRAG supports three retrieval modes:\n1. Local Retrieval: Focuses on entity ego-networks and multi-hop path traversal. 2. Global Retrieval: Synthesizes high-level thematic abstracts across community clusters. 3. Hybrid Retrieval: Uses Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) to blend local paths, community summaries, and BM25 chunk evidence.",
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "metadata": {
        "doc_id": "enterprise_brief"
      },
      "token_count": 44
    },
    {
      "id": "enterprise_brief_chunk_3",
      "text": "Nexus-GraphRAG integrates with EvalGuard AI to evaluate RAG faithfulness, answer relevance, and context recall. It also pairs with SynthoTab for privacy-preserving synthetic dataset generation using Differential Privacy. Finally, Nexus-GraphRAG exports standalone, responsive dark-mode HTML reports with interactive force graphs.",
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "metadata": {
        "doc_id": "enterprise_brief"
      },
      "token_count": 39
    }
  ],
